<circle cx=\"190\" cy=\"40\" r=\"3\" fill=\"#4169e1\" stroke=\"#4169e1\"></circle><line x1=\"190\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"190\" y2=\"120\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-dasharray=\"3\"></line><line x1=\"190\" y1=\"40\" x2=\"30\" y2=\"40\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-dasharray=\"3\"></line><foreignObject x=\"14\" y=\"120\" width=\"14\" height=\"18\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mi>O</mi></math></div></foreignObject></svg><figcaption>The tangent (blue) and normal (green) to <math><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mi>x</mi></msqrt></mrow></math> at (4, 2).</figcaption></figure>","hidden":true,"type":"code"},{"input":"!!! example\n\t\n\tThe slope of the tangent at ``\\left(4,2\\right)`` is\n\n\t```math\n\t\\begin{aligned}\n\tm=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{\\sqrt{4+h}-2}{h}&=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{\\left(\\sqrt{4+h}-2\\right)\\left(\\sqrt{4+h}+2\\right)}{h\\left(\\sqrt{4+h}+2\\right)}\\\\\n\t&=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{4+h-4}{h\\left(\\sqrt{4+h}+2\\right)}\\\\\n\t&=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4+h}+2}=\\frac{1}{4}\n\t\\end{aligned}\n\t```\n\n\tThe tangent line has equations\n\n\t```math\n\ty=\\frac{1}{4}\\left(x-4\\right)+2\\quad\\textrm{or}\\quad x-4y+4=0\n\t```\n\n\tand the normal has slope ``-4`` and, therefore, equation\n\n\t```math\n\ty=-4\\left(x-4\\right)+2\\quad\\textrm{or}\\quad 4x+y-18=0\n\t```\n\n","output":"","result":"!!! example\n\t\n\tThe slope of the tangent at ``\\left(4,2\\right)`` is\n\n\t```math\n\t\\begin{aligned}\n\tm=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{\\sqrt{4+h}-2}{h}&=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{\\left(\\sqrt{4+h}-2\\right)\\left(\\sqrt{4+h}+2\\right)}{h\\left(\\sqrt{4+h}+2\\right)}\\\\\n\t&=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{4+h-4}{h\\left(\\sqrt{4+h}+2\\right)}\\\\\n\t&=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4+h}+2}=\\frac{1}{4}\n\t\\end{aligned}\n\t```\n\n\tThe tangent line has equations\n\n\t```math\n\ty=\\frac{1}{4}\\left(x-4\\right)+2\\quad\\textrm{or}\\quad x-4y+4=0\n\t```\n\n\tand the normal has slope ``-4`` and, therefore, equation\n\n\t```math\n\ty=-4\\left(x-4\\right)+2\\quad\\textrm{or}\\quad 4x+y-18=0\n\t```\n\n","resultHTML":"<aside class=\"markdown-admonition markdown-admonition-example\"><div class=\"markdown-admonition-title\">Example</div><div class=\"markdown-admonition-body\"><p>The slope of the tangent at <math><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mn>4,2</mn><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></math> is</p>\n<math display=\"block\" class=\"tml-display\" style=\"display:block math;\"><mtable displaystyle=\"true\" class=\"tml-jot\"><mtr><mtd class=\"tml-right\" style=\"padding-left:0em;padding-right:0em;\"><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mspace width=\"0.1667em\"></mspace><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>h</mi></mfrac></mrow></mtd><mtd class=\"tml-left\" style=\"padding-left:0em;padding-right:0em;\"><mrow><mo>=</mo><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mspace width=\"0.1667em\"></mspace><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class=\"tml-right\" style=\"padding-left:0em;padding-right:0em;\"><mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class=\"tml-left\" style=\"padding-left:0em;padding-right:0em;\"><mrow><mo>=</mo><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mspace width=\"0.1667em\"></mspace><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class=\"tml-right\" style=\"padding-left:0em;padding-right:0em;\"><mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class=\"tml-left\" style=\"padding-left:0em;padding-right:0em;\"><mrow><mo>=</mo><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mspace width=\"0.1667em\"></mspace><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></math>\n<p>The tangent line has equations</p>\n<math display=\"block\" class=\"tml-display\" style=\"display:block math;\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mtext>or</mtext><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>\n<p>and the normal has slope <math><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"false\">−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></math> and, therefore, equation</p>\n<math display=\"block\" class=\"tml-display\" style=\"display:block math;\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"false\">−</mo><mn>4</mn><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mtext>or</mtext><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>18</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math></div></aside>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{},"translationSource":null},{"input":"## The Derivative\n\nA straight line has the property that its slope is the same at all points. For any other graph, however, the slope may vary from point to point. Thus, the slope of the graph of ``y=f\\left(x\\right)`` at the point ``x`` is itself a function of ``x``. At any point ``x`` where the graph has a finite slope, we say that ``f`` is *differentiable*, and we call the slope the *derivative* of ``f``. The derivative is therefore the limit of the Newton quotient.\n\n!!! definition\n\tThe derivative of a function ``f`` is another function ``f^\\prime`` defined by\n\t```math\n\tf^\\prime\\left(x\\right)=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{f\\left(x+h\\right)-f\\left(x\\right)}{h}\n\t```\n\tat all points ``x`` for which the limit exists (i.e., is a finite real number). If ``f^\\prime`` exists, we say that ``f`` is differentiable at ``x``.\n\nThe domain of the derivative ``f^\\prime`` (read “``f`` prime”) is the set of numbers ``x`` in the domain of ``f`` where the graph of ``f`` has a nonvertical tangent line, and the value ``f^\\prime\\left(x_0\\right)`` of ``f^\\prime`` at such a point ``x_0`` is the slope of the tangent line to ``y=f\\left(x\\right)`` there. Thus, the equation of the tangent line to ``y=\\left(x\\right)`` at ``f\\left(x_0\\right)`` is\n\n```math\ny=f\\left(x_0\\right)+f^\\prime\\left(x_0\\right)\\left(x-x_0\\right)\n```\n\nThe domain ``f^\\prime`` may be smaller than the domain of ``f`` because it contains only those points in the domain of ``f`` at which ``f`` is differentiable. Values of ``x`` in the domain of ``f`` where ``f`` is not differentiable and that are not endpoints of the domain of ``f`` are *singular points* of ``f``.\n\nThe value of the derivative of ``f`` at a particular point ``x_0`` can be expressed as a limit in either of two ways:\n\n```math\nf^\\prime\\left(x_0\\right)=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{f\\left(x_0+h\\right)-f\\left(x_0\\right)}{h}=\\lim_{x\\to x_0}\\frac{f\\left(x\\right)-f\\left(x_0\\right)}{x-x_0}\n```\nIn the second limit ``x_0+h`` is replaced by ``x``, so that ``h=x-x_0`` and ``h\\to 0`` is equivalent to ``x\\to x_0``.\n\nThe process of calculating the derivative ``f^\\prime`` of a given function ``f`` is called *differentiation*.","output":"","result":"## The Derivative\n\nA straight line has the property that its slope is the same at all points. For any other graph, however, the slope may vary from point to point. Thus, the slope of the graph of ``y=f\\left(x\\right)`` at the point ``x`` is itself a function of ``x``. At any point ``x`` where the graph has a finite slope, we say that ``f`` is *differentiable*, and we call the slope the *derivative* of ``f``. The derivative is therefore the limit of the Newton quotient.\n\n!!! definition\n\tThe derivative of a function ``f`` is another function ``f^\\prime`` defined by\n\t```math\n\tf^\\prime\\left(x\\right)=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{f\\left(x+h\\right)-f\\left(x\\right)}{h}\n\t```\n\tat all points ``x`` for which the limit exists (i.e., is a finite real number). If ``f^\\prime`` exists, we say that ``f`` is differentiable at ``x``.\n\nThe domain of the derivative ``f^\\prime`` (read “``f`` prime”) is the set of numbers ``x`` in the domain of ``f`` where the graph of ``f`` has a nonvertical tangent line, and the value ``f^\\prime\\left(x_0\\right)`` of ``f^\\prime`` at such a point ``x_0`` is the slope of the tangent line to ``y=f\\left(x\\right)`` there. Thus, the equation of the tangent line to ``y=\\left(x\\right)`` at ``f\\left(x_0\\right)`` is\n\n```math\ny=f\\left(x_0\\right)+f^\\prime\\left(x_0\\right)\\left(x-x_0\\right)\n```\n\nThe domain ``f^\\prime`` may be smaller than the domain of ``f`` because it contains only those points in the domain of ``f`` at which ``f`` is differentiable. Values of ``x`` in the domain of ``f`` where ``f`` is not differentiable and that are not endpoints of the domain of ``f`` are *singular points* of ``f``.\n\nThe value of the derivative of ``f`` at a particular point ``x_0`` can be expressed as a limit in either of two ways:\n\n```math\nf^\\prime\\left(x_0\\right)=\\lim_{h\\to 0}\\frac{f\\left(x_0+h\\right)-f\\left(x_0\\right)}{h}=\\lim_{x\\to x_0}\\frac{f\\left(x\\right)-f\\left(x_0\\right)}{x-x_0}\n```\nIn the second limit ``x_0+h`` is replaced by ``x``, so that ``h=x-x_0`` and ``h\\to 0`` is equivalent to ``x\\to x_0``.\n\nThe process of calculating the derivative ``f^\\prime`` of a given function ``f`` is called *differentiation*.","resultHTML":"<h2 id=\"md-y2ubvb-1526-1db13wd-the-derivative\">The Derivative</h2>\n<p>A straight line has the property that its slope is the same at all points. For any other graph, however, the slope may vary from point to point. Thus, the slope of the graph of <math><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></math> at the point <math><mi>x</mi></math> is itself a function of <math><mi>x</mi></math>. At any point <math><mi>x</mi></math> where the graph has a finite slope, we say that <math><mi>f</mi></math> is <em>differentiable</em>, and we call the slope the <em>derivative</em> of <math><mi>f</mi></math>. The derivative is therefore the limit of the Newton quotient.</p>\n<aside class=\"markdown-admonition markdown-admonition-definition\"><div class=\"markdown-admonition-title\">Definition</div><div class=\"markdown-admonition-body\"><p>The derivative of a function <math><mi>f</mi></math> is another function <math><msup><mi>f</mi><mo class=\"tml-prime tml-lrg-pad\">′</mo></msup></math> defined by</p>\n<math display=\"block\" class=\"tml-display\" style=\"display:block math;\"><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo class=\"tml-prime tml-lrg-pad\">′</mo></msup><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mspace width=\"0.1667em\"></mspace><mfrac><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></mfrac></mrow></math>\n<p>at all points <math><mi>x</mi></math> for which the limit exists (i.e., is a finite real number). If <math><msup><mi>f</mi><mo class=\"tml-prime tml-lrg-pad\">′</mo></msup></math> exists, we say that <math><mi>f</mi></math> is differentiable at <math><mi>x</mi></math>.</p></div></aside>\n<p>The domain of the derivative <math><msup><mi>f</mi><mo class=\"tml-prime tml-lrg-pad\">′</mo></msup></math> (read “<math><mi>f</mi></math> prime”) is the set of numbers <math><mi>x</mi></math> in the domain of <math><mi>f</mi></math> where the graph of <math><mi>f</mi></math> has a nonvertical tangent line, and the value <math><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo class=\"tml-prime tml-lrg-pad\">′</mo></msup><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></math> of <math><msup><mi>f</mi><mo class=\"tml-prime tml-lrg-pad\">′</mo></msup></math> at such a point <math><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math> is the slope of the tangent line to <math><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></math> there. Thus, the equation of the tangent line to <math><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></math> at <math><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></math> is</p>\n<math display=\"block\" class=\"tml-display\" style=\"display:block math;\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo class=\"tml-prime tml-lrg-pad\">′</mo></msup><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></math>\n<p>The domain <math><msup><mi>f</mi><mo class=\"tml-prime tml-lrg-pad\">′</mo></msup></math> may be smaller than the domain of <math><mi>f</mi></math> because it contains only those points in the domain of <math><mi>f</mi></math> at which <math><mi>f</mi></math> is differentiable. Values of <math><mi>x</mi></math> in the domain of <math><mi>f</mi></math> where <math><mi>f</mi></math> is not differentiable and that are not endpoints of the domain of <math><mi>f</mi></math> are <em>singular points</em> of <math><mi>f</mi></math>.</p>\n<p>The value of the derivative of <math><mi>f</mi></math> at a particular point <math><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math> can be expressed as a limit in either of two ways:</p>\n<math display=\"block\" class=\"tml-display\" style=\"display:block math;\"><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo class=\"tml-prime tml-lrg-pad\">′</mo></msup><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mspace width=\"0.1667em\"></mspace><mfrac><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><munder><mi>lim</mi><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>→</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></munder><mo>⁡</mo><mspace width=\"0.1667em\"></mspace><mfrac><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>\n<p>In the second limit <math><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></math> is replaced by <math><mi>x</mi></math>, so that <math><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></math> and <math><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math> is equivalent to <math><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>→</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></math>.</p>\n<p>The process of calculating the derivative <math><msup><mi>f</mi><mo class=\"tml-prime tml-lrg-pad\">′</mo></msup></math> of a given function <math><mi>f</mi></math> is called <em>differentiation</em>.</p>","hidden":true,"type":"markdown","translations":{},"translationSource":null},{"input":"const scale = 40;\nconst fontX = 16;\nconst fontY = 22;\n\nconst figure = JSCells.figure({\n    width: 13 * scale,\n    height: 9 * scale,\n    caption: \"Graphical differentiation.\",\n});\n\nfunction addLine(x1, y1, x2, y2, { stroke = \"#000000\", width = 1, dash } = {}) {\n    const element = figure.line()\n        .x1(x1).y1(y1)\n        .x2(x2).y2(y2)\n        .stroke(stroke)\n        .strokeWidth(width);\n\n    if (dash !== undefined) element.setAttribute(\"stroke-dasharray\", dash);\n}\n\nfunction addCircle(cx, cy, radius, fill, stroke) {\n    figure.circle()\n        .cx(cx).cy(cy).r(radius)\n        .fill(fill).stroke(stroke);\n}\n\nfunction addMathLabel(value, x, y, width, height = fontY) {\n    figure.math()\n        .x(x).y(y)\n        .width(width).height(height)\n        .latex(value);\n}\n\nfunction drawAxes(width, height, originX, originY, shiftX, shiftY, xTicks, yTicks) {\n    const axisEndX = shiftX + width - 3;\n    const axisTopY = shiftY + 3;\n\n    addLine(shiftX, originY, axisEndX, originY);\n    figure.polygon()\n        .points(`${axisEndX},${originY} ${axisEndX - 6},${originY - 3} ${axisEndX - 6},${originY + 3}`)\n        .fill(\"#000000\");\n\n    addLine(originX, shiftY + height, originX, axisTopY);\n    figure.polygon()\n        .points(`${originX},${axisTopY} ${originX - 3},${axisTopY + 6} ${originX + 3},${axisTopY + 6}`)\n        .fill(\"#000000\");\n\n    addMathLabel(\"O\", originX - fontX - 2, originY, fontX);\n    addMathLabel(\"x\", shiftX + width - fontX - 2, originY - fontY - 2, fontX);\n    addMathLabel(\"y\", originX + 2, shiftY - 2, fontX);\n\n    for (const value of xTicks) {\n        const x = originX + scale * value;\n        addLine(x, originY - 3, x, originY + 3);\n\n        const label = String(value);\n        const labelWidth = fontX * label.length;\n        addMathLabel(label, x - labelWidth / 2, originY, labelWidth);\n    }\n\n    for (const value of yTicks) {\n        const y = originY - scale * value;\n        addLine(originX - 3, y, originX + 3, y);\n\n        const label = String(value);\n        const labelWidth = fontX * label.length;\n        addMathLabel(label, originX - labelWidth, y - fontY / 2, labelWidth);\n    }\n}\n\nfunction plotXY(fn, from, to, originX, originY, { color = \"#ff0000\", width = 1, dots = [] } = {}) {\n    const intervals = Math.round((to - from) / 0.01);\n    const points = [];\n\n    for (let index = 0; index <= intervals; index += 1) {\n        const x = from + (to - from) * index / intervals;\n        points.push(`${originX + scale * x},${originY - scale * fn(x)}`);\n    }\n\n    figure.polyline()\n        .points(points.join(\" \"))\n        .fill(\"none\")\n        .stroke(color)\n        .strokeWidth(width);\n\n    for (const x of dots) {\n        addCircle(originX + scale * x, originY - scale * fn(x), 3, color, color);\n    }\n}\n\nconst panelWidth = 6 * scale;\nconst panelHeight = 4 * scale;\n\n// Top-left: piecewise linear function\ndrawAxes(panelWidth, panelHeight, 3 * scale, 2 * scale, 0, 0, [-1, 1], [-1, 1]);\nplotXY((x) => -x - 2, -2, -1, 3 * scale, 2 * scale);\nplotXY((x) => x, -1, 1, 3 * scale, 2 * scale);\nplotXY((x) => -x + 2, 1, 2, 3 * scale, 2 * scale);\n\n// Top-right: -sin(x) and its tangent lines\ndrawAxes(panelWidth, panelHeight, 10 * scale, 2 * scale, 7 * scale, 0, [-1, 1], [-1, 1]);\nplotXY((x) => -Math.sin(x), -3, 3, 10 * scale, 2 * scale, { dots: [-1, 1] });\nplotXY(\n    (x) => -Math.cos(-1) * (x + 1) - Math.sin(-1),\n    -2, 0, 10 * scale, 2 * scale,\n    { color: \"#4169e1\" },\n);\nplotXY(\n    (x) => -Math.cos(1) * (x - 1) - Math.sin(1),\n    0, 2, 10 * scale, 2 * scale,\n    { color: \"#4169e1\" },\n);\n\n// Bottom-left: step function with open endpoints\ndrawAxes(panelWidth, panelHeight, 3 * scale, 7 * scale, 0, 5 * scale, [-1, 1], [-1, 1]);\nplotXY(() => -1, -2, -1, 3 * scale, 7 * scale);\nplotXY(() => 1, -1, 1, 3 * scale, 7 * scale);\nplotXY(() => -1, 1, 2, 3 * scale, 7 * scale);\n\nfor (const [x, y] of [\n    [-1, -1],\n    [-1, 1],\n    [1, -1],\n    [1, 1],\n]) {\n    addCircle(3 * scale + x * scale, 7 * scale - y * scale, 3, \"#ffffff\", \"#ff0000\");\n}\n\n// Bottom-right: -cos(x) and marked tangent segments\ndrawAxes(panelWidth, panelHeight, 10 * scale, 7 * scale, 7 * scale, 5 * scale, [-1, 1], [-1, 1]);\nplotXY((x) => -Math.cos(x), -3, 3, 10 * scale, 7 * scale, { dots: [-1, 1] });\n\n// Dashed vertical guides\nfor (const x of [2 * scale, 4 * scale, 9 * scale, 11 * scale]) {\n    addLine(x, 0, x, 9 * scale, { dash: \"3\" });\n}\n\naddLine(9 * scale, 7 * scale + Math.cos(-1) * scale, 9 * scale, 7 * scale, {\n    stroke: \"#4169e1\",\n});\naddLine(11 * scale, 7 * scale + Math.cos(1) * scale, 11 * scale, 7 * scale, {\n    stroke: \"#4169e1\",\n});\n\nfigure;","output":"","result":"Oxy−11−11Oxy−11−11Oxy−11−11Oxy−11−11Graphical differentiation.","resultHTML":"<figure><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"520\" height=\"360\" viewBox=\"0 0 520 360\"><line x1=\"0\" y1=\"80\" x2=\"237\" y2=\"80\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"></line><polygon points=\"237,80 231,77 231,83\" fill=\"#000000\"></polygon><line x1=\"120\" y1=\"160\" x2=\"120\" y2=\"3\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"></line><polygon points=\"120,3 117,9 123,9\" fill=\"#000000\"></polygon><foreignObject x=\"102\" y=\"80\" width=\"16\" height=\"22\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mi>O</mi></math></div></foreignObject><foreignObject x=\"222\" y=\"56\" width=\"16\" height=\"22\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mi>x</mi></math></div></foreignObject><foreignObject x=\"122\" y=\"-2\" width=\"16\" height=\"22\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mi>y</mi></math></div></foreignObject><line x1=\"80\" y1=\"77\" x2=\"80\" y2=\"83\" stroke=\"#000000\" stroke-width=\"1\"></line><foreignObject x=\"64\" y=\"80\" width=\"32\" height=\"22\"><div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><math><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math></div></foreignObject><line x1=\"160\" y1=\"77\" x2=\"160\" y2=\"83\" stro